title: "ERP Subsidies 2026: What Is Left to Scope an Odoo Project?"
lang: "en"
publishedAt: "2026-11-20"
category: "Project Management"
excerpt: "Wallonia's cheque and Brussels' Consultancy grant are suspended: the aid still open in late 2026 to scope an Odoo project, and the signature trap."
---

You are preparing the 2027 budget for an ERP project. You have read a 2025 article promising a 50% subsidy on your scoping phase. Do not count on it.

Two forms of aid that many business owners relied on are no longer available for new applications. Here is what is closed, what is still open, and the timing mistake that makes you lose the aid.

## What is suspended

**In Wallonia: the "digital maturity" cheque.**

It has been suspended since 12 July 2026.

No new applications can be submitted. Applications already submitted before that date are not cancelled.

It was the aid closest to ERP scoping: a digital assessment, followed by an implementation plan.

An overhaul has been announced. According to a specialist website, the Walloon decree of 2 July 2026 reforms the business cheques from 1 July 2027. The rates and caps of the future digital cheque are not known.

**In Brussels: the Consultancy grant.**

Since 12 August 2026, the Region has suspended its consultancy, training, recruitment and coworking grants.

Applications submitted before that date continue to be processed and paid under the rules in force.

The measure is presented as temporary. One relay site mentions a suspension until the end of 2026. I have found no official reopening date. Do not budget on it.

## What is still open at the end of 2026

This is the position as at 20 November 2026. Rates and caps vary from one source to another: check them on the official websites before committing a single euro.

| Region | Aid | Status | What it funds | Rates and cap found |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Brussels | Digitalisation grant | Open | External consultancy assignment: digitalisation of internal processes, IT security, website | 25 to 70%; €10,000 per year |
| Wallonia | Cybersecurity cheque | Open | Security audit and support, via an accredited provider | 75% excl. VAT; €50,000 excl. VAT over 3 years |
| Wallonia | Training cheque (Forem) | Open | Training hours with an approved provider | €15 paid by the company for a €30 cheque |
| Wallonia | Digital maturity cheque | **Suspended** (12 July 2026) | Digital diagnostic and plan | — |
| Brussels | Consultancy grant | **Suspended** (12 August 2026) | General external consultancy | — |

For the Digitalisation grant, the gap in rates between sources is easily explained.

The base rate is 25%, rising to as much as 70% with uplifts.

These uplifts depend on the company's profile and size. The sources showing 50% describe a particular case, not the rule.

## The Digitalisation grant: the aid that matters for scoping

It is the only one of the three that really targets a process project. The official rules:

- The assignment must concern the digitalisation of internal processes, or IT security.
- It must last 6 months at most.
- The grant is at least €500 and at most €10,000 per assignment.
- The cap is €10,000 per year and two subsidised assignments per calendar year.
- The consultant must have been carrying out consultancy activities for at least 2 years.

Two points deserve attention. First, the grant funds a consultancy assignment. An Odoo scoping phase (process analysis, specifications, choice of scope) fits that logic. Licences and development, however, are not mentioned in the texts I consulted, so I cannot say they are covered. Have the scope of your quote confirmed by Bruxelles Économie et Emploi.

Second, the grant is taxable: it counts as part of the company's taxable income. Budget for it net of tax.

## The trap: signing too early

This is the costliest mistake. If you sign and then start work, the aid is lost.

In Brussels, the rule is clear: the application must be submitted via MonBEE no later than the day before the assignment starts. The assignment must then start no later than 3 months after notification of the award. The response time is long: up to 4 months after receipt of your complete application. You therefore need to build it into your schedule.

In practice:

1. Obtain the scoping quote, but do not let the work start.
2. Submit the application on MonBEE with that quote.
3. Wait for the decision before launching the assignment.
4. Align the project schedule with this timeline, not the other way round.

A signed quote is not necessarily a start. But the safest course is to launch nothing before the decision, and to ask Bruxelles Économie et Emploi what counts as the "start of the assignment".

## Wallonia: narrow options

For ERP scoping, the cybersecurity cheque does not fund your project. It does not fund an AI project as such, nor the choice of an ERP. It becomes useful if your project includes a security audit. Another constraint: the company must use an accredited provider. However, accreditations have been frozen since 17 July 2025. Check, therefore, that your provider is already accredited for this cheque.

The training cheque is for training your teams, not for paying for scoping. On the official Wallonia website, the subsidy is €15 per cheque, which therefore costs you only €15.

The number of cheques per year depends on the size of the company. One rule to remember: you must link the cheques to the training before the first lesson. It is the same logic as in Brussels: the order of the steps decides the aid.

Sources diverge on what comes next. An initial announcement mentioned a rate of €25 per hour from September 2026. A publication dated 20 November states that the new "Capital Formation" schemes will be available from 1 September 2027. For 2027, plan on the current scheme.

## What I would do in your place

- **Brussels:** budget the scoping phase with the Digitalisation grant as an assumption, not a certainty. Prepare a scenario without aid.
- **Wallonia:** budget the scoping phase without a subsidy. Keep the cybersecurity cheque for a security component, and the training cheque for getting your teams up to speed.
- **Everywhere:** re-read the official page on the day you apply. The 2026 rules have changed three times in five months.

Official sources to consult: [Chèques-entreprises](https://www.cheques-entreprises.be/), [Bruxelles Économie et Emploi](https://economie-emploi.brussels/prime-digitalisation) and [the Forem](https://www.wallonie.be/fr/demarches/se-former-grace-aux-cheques-formations).

